.TH EMBER 8 "October 26, 2026" "ember 2.5-1" "Ember Manual"
.SH NAME
ember \- AUR helper and pacman wrapper for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ember
.RB [ \-y ]
.RB [ \-\-keep\-deps ]
.RB [ \-\-review ]
.br
.B ember
.RI [ options ]
.B install
.IR package " ..."
.br
.B ember
.RI [ options ]
.BR remove " | " purge
.IR package " ..."
.br
.B ember
.B search
.IR term " ..."
.br
.B ember
.B clean
.br
.B ember
.B list
.br
.B ember
.BR \-h " | " \-v
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ember
is an AUR helper with a
.BR pacman (8)
wrapper.
It installs, upgrades, removes and searches packages from both the official
repositories and the Arch User Repository (AUR) through a single interface.
.PP
Every transaction is first shown as a table of packages with their versions
and sizes, followed by a summary and a
.B [Y/n]
question.
Nothing is changed until the question is answered with yes.
.PP
The command
.B emb
is a shorthand for
.B ember
and behaves identically.
It is a symbolic link to the same program.
.PP
.B ember
must not be run as root.
It calls
.BR sudo (8)
whenever it needs elevated privileges, and
.BR makepkg (8)
refuses to run as root anyway.
.PP
When
.B ember
is run without a command, it updates the system and all installed AUR
packages.
.SS Prompts
Prompts are answered with the keyboard.
Pressing
.B y
or
.B n
moves the highlighted letter between
.B Y
and
.BR N .
Tab, space and the left and right arrow keys toggle it as well.
Enter confirms the highlighted choice and Ctrl-C aborts.
.SS AUR packages
Packages that are not found in the repositories are looked up in the AUR.
Dependencies are resolved recursively, with runtime and build dependencies
tracked separately.
Dependencies available in the repositories are installed with
.BR pacman (8),
and the remaining ones are built from the AUR first.
.PP
Packages are built with
.BR makepkg (8)
inside the cache directory and the output is hidden.
A live progress list shows every package together with what it is currently
doing, such as downloading sources, compiling, packaging or installing.
The complete output of each step is written to a log file, and the last lines
are printed if a step fails.
.PP
Build dependencies that were only needed for building, and that nothing else
on the system requires, are removed again once everything is installed.
Use
.B \-\-keep\-deps
to keep them.
.PP
Packages that other AUR packages depend on are installed as soon as they are
built, because they are needed for the next build.
The remaining packages, together with any repository packages that were not
needed for building, are collected and installed after one final confirmation
that lists everything.
If that confirmation is declined, nothing from the final batch is installed.
The built packages stay in the cache, so the next run does not rebuild them.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "(none)" ", " update ", " upgrade ", " -Syu
Refresh the package databases with
.BR "pacman \-Sy" ,
then upgrade all repository packages and all installed AUR packages whose
version in the AUR is newer, according to
.BR vercmp (8).
Repository and AUR upgrades are shown in one table and confirmed together.
.TP
.BR install ", " ins ", " add ", " -S " " \fIpackage\fR " ..."
Install packages from the repositories or the AUR.
Packages that are already installed are skipped.
If a name cannot be found in either place, nothing is installed.
.TP
.BR remove ", " rm ", " uninstall ", " del ", " -R " " \fIpackage\fR " ..."
Remove packages.
Afterwards the dependencies that became unused are listed and a separate
question asks whether they should be removed as well.
.TP
.BR purge " " \fIpackage\fR " ..."
Like
.BR remove ,
but also removes configuration backup files, as
.B pacman \-Rn
does.
.TP
.BR search ", " s ", " find " " \fIterm\fR " ..."
Search the repositories and the AUR.
Several terms must all match.
Terms are treated as regular expressions where possible, and matches are
highlighted.
Installed packages are marked, and AUR results show their votes and whether
they are flagged out of date.
At most 30 AUR results are shown, ordered by votes.
.TP
.B clean
Show the size of every cache and, after confirmation, empty them.
This covers the built AUR packages, the AUR sources, the build logs and the
package cache of
.BR pacman (8).
.TP
.B list, -Q
Creates a list of all installed packages. Can be used to search for installed packages.
.TP
.B help
Show a short usage summary.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes at every prompt.
The aliases
.B \-\-assume\-yes
and
.B \-\-noconfirm
are accepted as well.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-deps
Do not remove AUR build dependencies after building.
.TP
.B \-\-review
Before anything is upgraded, installed or built, open every AUR
.I PKGBUILD
and any
.I *.install
scripts in the pager and ask whether to continue.
This also applies to packages that are already cached.
The version that was reviewed is the version that gets built.
This question is not skipped by
.BR \-y .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory of the cache.
Defaults to
.IR ~/.cache .
.TP
.B PAGER
Pager used by
.BR \-\-review .
Defaults to
.BR less (1).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, colours are disabled.
Colours are also disabled when the output is not a terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ember/pkg/
Built AUR packages.
A package is reused when its version matches the one in the AUR.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ember/build/
Git clones of AUR packages and their downloaded sources.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ember/logs/
Logs of builds, installs and cleanups, one file per step.
.TP
.I /var/cache/pacman/pkg/
Package cache of
.BR pacman (8)
for repository packages, which is also emptied by
.BR clean .
.SH EXAMPLES
Update the system and all AUR packages:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ ember
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install a repository package and an AUR package together:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ emb ins konsole lunar-client
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read the build scripts before installing an AUR package:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ ember install \-\-review lunar\-client
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove a package and then choose whether to remove its dependencies:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ ember remove konsole
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search the repositories and the AUR:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ ember search terminal emulator
.fi
.RE
.PP
Empty all caches:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ ember clean
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR less (1),
.BR PKGBUILD (5),
.BR pacman.conf (5),
.BR makepkg (8),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR vercmp (8)
